\caption(Local averaging reproduces constants, not arbitrary lines. Gaussian weights remain numerically usable far from the data, where nearest distance and effective sample size reveal the limited support.)
\alttext(A straight true line and a curved local-constant fit disagree at the boundaries. A second panel shows the local effective sample size peaking near the centre.)

>> Duplicates and incomplete validation coverage

Use \(x=(0,0,10)\), \(y=(0,2,100)\) and a raw-unit uniform window. At \(h=0.1\),
ordinary predictions at x=0 average the two responses to one; they cannot interpolate both.
Deleting one duplicate leaves the other, giving predictions two and zero. Deleting the
isolated x=10 row leaves no support. Conditional deletion MSE is only four on two rows,
so silently omitting the third row would make this candidate look excellent.

At \(h=11\), every deletion has both remaining observations available. Predictions
are 51, 50 and 1, giving full-coverage MSE \((51^2+48^2+99^2)/3=4902\).
The objective correctly treats the incomplete h=0.1 candidate as ineligible, rather than
pretending that four and 4902 measure the same validation experiment.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kreg_coverage.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;d.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{0,0,10});d.add_column("y",std::vector<double>{0,2,100});dm::stats::KernelRegressionOptions o;o.kernel=dm::stats::KernelRegressionKernel::Uniform;o.bandwidth=.1;o.standardize=false;const dm::stats::KernelRegression narrow(d,"y ~ x",o);
  o.bandwidth=-1;o.bandwidth_candidates={.1,11};const dm::stats::KernelRegression selected(d,"y ~ x",o);const auto path=selected.bandwidth_diagnostics();
  auto points=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),coverage=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();points.points({0,0,10},{0,2,100},"training",{37,99,235}).title("Two duplicates and one isolated point").x_label("x").y_label("response").x_limits(-1,11).y_limits(-10,140);
  coverage.bars({1,2},path.numeric_column("coverage").values(),"LOO coverage",{37,99,235},.5).title("Bandwidth candidates cover different rows").x_label("1: h=0.1; 2: h=11").y_label("fraction predicted").x_limits(.5,2.5).y_limits(0,1.4);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(points).add(coverage).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/kreg_coverage.svg");
  std::print("Narrow-window training diagnostics:\n\n{}\n\nSearch, chosen h = {}:\n\n{}\n",narrow.training_details().select({"row","actual","full_fit","loo_fit","leverage"}).to_md(6),selected.bandwidth(),path.to_md(6));
}
```
