\alttext(Two observations share x zero while a third is far away at x ten. Candidate coverage rises from two-thirds at the narrow window to one at the broad window; tables retain the missing prediction and infinite selection objective.)

> Checking the theory on a known function

We fix 31 equally spaced predictor locations in [0,1], the target \(m(x)=\sin(2\pi x)\)
and deterministic contamination \(0.2\cos(20\pi x)\). This is a transparent finite-design
stress check, not a random-noise Monte Carlo experiment or an estimate of statistical
bias and variance. Training responses contain the oscillation, while the dense reference
grid uses the known smooth target. Every candidate uses the same raw-coordinate bandwidth,
training design and complete Gaussian deletion coverage.

We compare apparent RMSE, conditional deletion RMSE against contaminated training responses,
and dense-grid RMSE against the true function. They are three different targets. The
selected bandwidth minimizes the declared deletion criterion, not the withheld function
error; their rankings need not agree. The same fixed data also show the deterioration
from excessive smoothing and the attraction of apparent interpolation at tiny h.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kreg_known_function.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
const auto x=dm::seql(0,1,31),truth=dm::sin(x*(2*std::acos(-1.0))),y=truth+.2*dm::cos(x*(20*std::acos(-1.0)));dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;d.add_column("x",x.values());d.add_column("y",y.values());
  const auto gx=dm::seql(0,1,301);dm::dstruct::DataFrame reference;reference.add_column("x",gx.values());reference.add_column("y",dm::sin(gx*(2*std::acos(-1.0))).values());
  dm::stats::KernelRegressionOptions o;o.standardize=false;o.bandwidth_candidates={.005,.01,.02,.04,.08,.16,.32,.64};const dm::stats::KernelRegression chosen(d,"y ~ x",o);dm::dstruct::DataFrame rows;std::vector<double> logh,apparent,loo,known;
  for(double h:o.bandwidth_candidates){o.bandwidth=h;const dm::stats::KernelRegression m(d,"y ~ x",o);auto row=m.model_summary().select({"bandwidth","apparent_rmse","loo_rmse"});row.add_column("true_function_rmse",std::vector<double>{m.score(reference).double_at("rmse",0)});rows=rows.ncols()?rows.concat_rows(row):row;logh.push_back(std::log10(h));apparent.push_back(row.double_at("apparent_rmse",0));loo.push_back(row.double_at("loo_rmse",0));known.push_back(row.double_at("true_function_rmse",0));}
  auto fit=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),loss=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();fit.points(x.values(),y.values(),"contaminated",{148,163,184}).lines(gx.values(),reference.numeric_column("y").values(),"known target",{0,0,0}).lines(gx.values(),chosen.predict(reference),"chosen fit",{37,99,235});fit.title("A known smooth target and fixed ripple").x_label("x").y_label("response").y_limits(-1.4,2);
  loss.lines(logh,apparent,"apparent",{22,163,74}).lines(logh,loo,"deleted responses",{220,38,38}).lines(logh,known,"known function",{37,99,235});loss.title("Three losses answer different questions").x_label("log10 bandwidth").y_label("RMSE").y_limits(0,1.1);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(fit).add(loss).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/kreg_known_function.svg");std::print("Chosen conditional-CV h = {}.\n\n{}\n",chosen.bandwidth(),rows.to_md(6));
}
```
